This work studies a lightweight static method for constructing Cryptographic Bills of Materials (CBoMs) directly from Java byte-code. The proposed system, FuzzyExtract, applies stack simulation and depth-bounded approximate call-graph analysis to identify cryptographic parameters without requiring full interprocedural reconstruction. The method focuses on locally observable bytecode patterns to recover algorithm names, key sizes, modes, and other values that define cryptographic behavior. An initial evaluation on a CryptoAPI-Bench dataset suggests that accurate CBoM extraction can be achieved on commodity hardware with modest computational cost.